Job Summary
Reporting to the Director, Institute for Human Development, and UZIMA DS Hub Directors, the Manager, UZIMA Research Hub will manage the research process and support the Principal Investigators and various project leads in ensuring all sub-projects within the hub are implemented according to the highest standards. Additionally, the Hub Manager will run the day to day administrative work of the hub. He/She will ensure all the teams are connected working collaboratively and on target, through timely and consistent communication. He/She will also support all grant management functions to ensure Hub teams and Subawardees synergize to deliver all activities. The Hub Manager will also facilitate engagement with multisectoral stakeholders to identify sustainable model dissemination pathways into target communities.
Responsibilities
Manage all research processes, ensuring all the projects within the hub follow laid down regulatory rules, keeping meticulous record of all research documents, and supporting junior research staff within the hub, by organizing training and mentoring opportunities;
Manage and coordinate the day to activities of the hub, ensuring that all the teams work collaboratively and on target;
Responsible for yearly planning and budgeting meeting, and close out activities, ensuring financial reports are submitted to donors on time;
Provide support in identifying and scheduling for learning and sharing opportunities among the hub teams and external stakeholders and foster teamwork;
In collaboration with Finance and Grants department, manage the Sub-award processing of onboarding, communication, funds transfers, and collaborative activities;
Facilitate the process of formation and substance of a Community Advisory Board; selection, invitations and Terms of Engagement, meetings, among others Spearhead all the community engagement activities and processes;
Ensure smooth communication and coordination among all partners (internal and external) for UZIMA;
Work closely with the AKIJ communication team to ensure project activities are profiled through the different channels of communication targeting all key stakeholders including women, parents, implementers and policy makers among others; and
Work collaboratively with the Communications Officer to package information for dissemination to different audience including policy makers, research communities and other audiences.
Requirements
Have a Master's Degree in Public Health, Mental Health, Maternal and Children Health, Psychology and other related fields. A Doctorate degree (PhD) in similar or related fields is an added advantage);
Have not less than 5 years of strong Research and Project Management, as well as Projects Coordination experience;
Experience coordinating or supporting a multi-disciplinary project with public health relevance is key to this role;
Have strong organizational, interpersonal, oral and communication skills;
Have practical experience working in a multi-cultural setting, with hands on experience in community mobilization and partner engagement processes;
Have demonstrable ability to document research study processes and outcomes, compile donor reports; and
Must be willing to travel outside the country.
Key Skills, Knowledge and Competencies:
Ability to work under minimal supervision;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills and a good team player;
Fluent in English and Kiswahili; and
Keen desire to learn and share knowledge.

JOB DESCRIPTION
The Managing Director is the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of KAGRC and shall be responsible to the Board of Directors for the implementation of KAGRC’s objectives and strategies for the realization of its goals. The holder shall also be responsible for the day to day operations and administration of the organization and the prudent management of its resources.
The duties and responsibilities shall include:
Ensuring development and review of policies, strategic plans, business plans and work plans;
Responsible for day-to-day running of the organisation;
Advising the Board on all policies and strategies relating to management of the organization;
Secretary to the Board and custodian of the KAGRC seal;
Ensuring proper interpretation and implementation of the Board’s decisions;
Monitoring implementation of Board’s decisions and appraising the Board on progress;
Ensuring linkage of KAGRC’s staffing to organizational objectives;
Providing leadership in developing, reviewing and implementing KAGRC strategic plans and ensuring its compliance with the Constitution, Kenya vision 2030 and other prevailing government policies;
Ensuring effective implementation of the mandate of the organization including gene banking of all livestock species (genomics) and benchmark on animal genetics worldwide;
Ensuring development and implementation of policies, strategies and internal control systems to ensure delivery of quality service to internal and external clients;
Ensuring development and implementation of an effective performance management framework for delivering the key priorities for KAGRC;
Leading in change management;
Effectively mobilizing resources for KAGRC activities;
Ensuring prudent management of KAGRC resources;
Planning, directing and coordinating the administrative and office support of the organization;
Coordinating and preparing business related proposals and resource mobilization for KAGRC as a reference point for genetic materials in partnership with the National Government and the Counties;
Ensuring effective communication between management and the Board, as well as between different levels of management and also stakeholders;
Providing leadership and fostering teamwork among employees;
Ensuring continuous achievement of KAGRC’s financial and operations strategic objectives in line with its uniqueness;
Managing corporate risk;
Initiating development of strategic partnerships and collaborations;
Ensuring development and approval of the budget;
Ensuring compliance with statutory obligations;
Fostering a culture that promotes ethical practice within the organization;
Ensuring succession management and employee growth and development; and
Any other duties assigned by the Board.
Job Specification
Bachelors degree in Veterinary Medicine (BVM), Animal Science or equivalent qualification from a recognized institution;
Masters degree in Veterinary Medicine, Animal breeding, Animal Science, Theriogenology or other relevant field;
Member of a professional body and in good standing;
Leadership course lasting not less than four (4) weeks from a recognized institution;
Demonstrated results in work performance;
At least fifteen (15) years’ work experience in a public or private institution;
At least five (5) years’ experience in senior management; and
Fulfilled the requirements of chapter six of the constitution.
KEY COMPETENCIES AND SKILLS
Strong analytical skills;
Strategic and innovative thinking;
Ability to mobilize resources;
Strong interpersonal skills;
Strong leadership skills; and
Negotiation skills.

Main Duties and Responsibilities
The duties and responsibilities are:
Operational Roles and Responsibilities
Handling external and internal communication directed to the General Manager;
Ensuring effective management of the General Managers diary and booking appointments for and on behalf
Supervising the support staff assigned to the General Manager
Organizing meetings and ensure the General Manager is well prepared for meetings;
Provide logistical support at various functions as assigned;
Maintain a proper document handling system in the office by keeping an efficient filing and retrieval system;
Attend to inquiries and liaise with the appropriate staff as necessary to ensure that needs are satisfactorily attended to;
Ensure the efficient and effective flow of communication between the office and customers, senior managers and other staff as appropriate;
Carrying out clerical duties e.g. filing and photocopying.
Perform any other relevant duties that may be assigned.
Knowledge and Skills Required:
The job holder must possess:
Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration or other related course;
Minimum two (2) year experience;
Must possess a high degree of confidentiality
Must demonstrate high integrity and ethical practice;
Must demonstrate ability to work independently with minimum supervision;
Must be a team player who is able to work cordially in teams;
Must demonstrate ability to multitask;
Must demonstrate commitment to operational effectiveness;
Should have ability to solve problems by applying relevant business knowledge;
Should demonstrate professional expertise in the relevant work area;
Must have the ability to communicate for both written and oral communication;
Must be able to work under pressure;
Must be a flexible person, who is willing to learn and able to work flexible hours to achieve goals;
Must have knowledge in use of MS office packages.
