About the role
Global Field Team supports Bolt’s operations, including its global entities, business stakeholders and other supporting functions for all product verticals such as Ride-Hailing, Rentals, Delivery, Bolt Market, Bolt Drive and Bolt Business from a local perspective. In close cooperation with Product Counsels (and members of other Legal, Risk and Procurement sub-teams, if needed), Global Field Team ensures that all existing and new products along with added features are legally compliant in given markets allocated to the respective Global Field Team members. When appropriate and needed, Global Field Team identifies and highlights legal risks and liabilities related thereto, in order for the relevant business stakeholders to understand potential legal implications for Bolt and its subsidiaries in order to take business decisions accordingly.
This team member is expected to (i) allow sharing of workload (ii) accept changes to the assigned markets and/or specific projects, as deemed necessary by the direct manager dependent on the growth of Bolt and workloads across teams, (iii) develop quickly to a level where he/she has autonomous ability to manage and resolve complex legal issues and projects and (iv) develop a strong legal and business acumen to understand when a matter escalation to the direct manager (and to Associate General Counsel and General Counsel, as instructed by the direct manager) is needed.
Your daily adventures will include:
Providing professional, timely and accurate business oriented legal support internally;
Identifying, monitoring and minimizing legal, regulatory and litigation risk and recommending appropriate policies, practices, and procedures across Legal Risk and Procurement team and Bolt;
Demonstrate technical legal expertise on projects showing a high degree of thought and critical analysis to identify root causes of the issues. Provide with appropriate legal options back to the client stakeholder in a presentation manner that is concise and effective to read;
Align skill and expertise profile with the Global Field Team Job Levelling Guide for calibration of expected quality standards and responsibilities of a legal counsel;
Proactive approach within Legal Risk and Procurement team as well as Global Field Team in order to advise colleagues across team on market-specific updates, escalations, increased risks and liabilities by using all forums applicable at Bolt (Slack, team meetings, emails, 1:1 and skip-level meetings);
Daily legal support to the assigned Bolt markets’ local subsidiaries and relevant local operations’ teams and senior team members, as the case may be, including but not limited to corporate law, employment law, commercial law and litigation;
Meeting the provided quarterly and/or annual budget for external law firms for local specific advice in given markets by managing the scope and instructions to the external law firms in a concise manner;
Draft and review commercial contracts, internal policies and procedures as instructed by senior team members and/or direct manager;
With the support and under supervision of senior team members, providing legal support for the expansion to new markets, including arranging completion of expansion questionnaires, internal assessment of thereof and managing the assigned budget for completing the task;
Legal support in implementing new products and features in relevant markets;
Monitor legal and regulatory developments in areas relevant to Bolt’s products in the assigned markets;
About you:
You have a Bachelor's Degree in Law or its equivalent
You have 4-6 years of post qualification legal practice experience at a law firm or an international company
You have completed your bar exams in one of the African jurisdictions in which Bolt operates or in a Commonwealth country
You have practical experience that ranges across commercial law, corporate law, dispute resolution, employment, consumer protection, competition law and intellectual property
You are well at home with legal aspects of marketing, privacy, intellectual property, consumer protection and the gig economy
You are organised. You deliver your work on time
You are creative, collaborative with a can-do attitude
You are flexible and open to dynamic environments
Experience is great, but what we really look for is drive, intelligence, and integrity. So even if you don’t tick every box, please consider applying if you feel you’re the kind of person described above!

